{
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Reason : 1 - The proposed installation of a front vehicle crossover to the house, provision of two associated front car parking bays and a replacement clear pedestrian path and alterations to the existing front boundary wall (with pillars and a pedestrian gate) would be unacceptable by reason of the proposal, because: \r\ni)\texceed the maximum private car parking standard for two to three bedroom houses with a Public Transport Accessibility Level of '3' located in Outer London, contrary to the sustainable transport objectives of London Plan Policy T6.1,\r\nii)\thaving a non-compliant inverse vehicle crossover layout (that would have a greater width adjoining the front garden's front boundary and narrower width adjoining the public footway) and excessively wide front vehicular entrance that would allow vehicles to access and egress the site via an unauthorised route across non-strengthened public footway surfacing and would harm the pedestrian safety and damage to highway conditions contrary to Local Plan Policies CC1, CC2 and EC2 and the Residential Crossovers and Off-Street Parking Policy.  \r\niii)\tnot ensuring a clear 2.4 metre wide visibility splay to each side of the vehicular opening and vehicle crossover without obstruction due to the adjoining front boundary wall and highway trees would risk the safety of pedestrians, cyclists and vehicle users contrary to Local Plan Policy EC2 and the Residential Crossovers and Off-Street Parking Policy.  \r\niv)\tthe proposal fails to provide drawings with correct driver sightline markings and adequate swept path analysis to demonstrate that its layout would not be harmful to highway safety, contrary to Local Plan Policy EC2 and the Residential Crossovers and Off-Street Parking Policy.  \r\nv)\tinadequate details to demonstrate that its hard landscaping design and materials would prevent additional surface water runoff flowing onto the public highway, contrary to Local Plan Policy EQ3 and the Council's Residential Crossovers and Off-Street Parking ",
    "Reason : 2 - The proposal, by reason of reduction to the house's historic front wall and pillars, loss of high quality soft landscaped green space, would be an intrusive development, out of character with the prevailing pattern of development in the locality, as well as having a serious and adverse effect on visual amenity, conservation area and ecology, contrary to Local Plan Policies GB7, CC1, CC2 and CC4.  "
  ],
